Deploying GitHub Actions Workflow to SuberTube Repository
📋 Overview
This guide walks you through deploying the automated error detection and fix workflow to your GitHub repository.

What gets deployed:

GitHub Actions workflow file (.github/workflows/fix-subertube-errors.yml)
Automated error detection (Gradle 9.6, Dependencies lock)
Automatic bugfix branch creation
Pull request generation with fixes pre-applied
Time Required: ~10 minutes

🚀 Quick Start (TL;DR)
# 1. Clone your repository
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/suber-tube.git
cd suber-tube

# 2. Create workflow directory
mkdir -p .github/workflows

# 3. Copy workflow file
cp github-workflow-fix-errors.yml .github/workflows/fix-subertube-errors.yml

# 4. Copy documentation
cp DEVELOPMENT-WORKFLOW.md .github/DEVELOPMENT-WORKFLOW.md
cp TROUBLESHOOTING-GUIDE.md .github/TROUBLESHOOTING-GUIDE.md

# 5. Commit and push
git add .github/
git commit -m "🤖 Add: GitHub Actions workflow for automated error detection and fixes"
git push origin develop

# 6. Verify in GitHub
# Visit: https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/suber-tube/settings/actions
📝 Step-by-Step Deployment
Step 1: Prepare Your Repository
1.1 Clone the repository locally

git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/suber-tube.git
cd suber-tube
git checkout develop
1.2 Verify repository structure

ls -la
# You should see:
# - android/          (Android source)
# - web/              (Web/Node.js source)
# - docs/             (Documentation)
# - README.md
# - SECURITY.md
# - etc.
1.3 Verify you have GitHub CLI installed (optional but helpful)

# macOS
