🧪 Testing the Workflow
Test 1: Verify Gradle Detection Works
1.1 Create test branch

git checkout -b test/gradle-9.6-error
1.2 Introduce Gradle 9.6 reference

# Modify gradle-wrapper.properties
sed -i.bak 's/gradle-8.4/gradle-9.6/g' \
  android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

# Verify change
grep gradle- android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
# Should show: gradle-9.6-bin.zip
1.3 Commit and push

git add android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
git commit -m "test: introduce gradle 9.6 error for workflow testing"
git push origin test/gradle-9.6-error
1.4 Watch workflow run

Visit: https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/suber-tube/actions
Expected:
✓ Workflow detects gradle-9.6 error
✓ Creates bugfix/gradle-9.6-compatibility branch
✓ Opens PR with fix
1.5 Clean up

# Revert test changes
git reset --hard HEAD~1
# Delete test branch
git push origin --delete test/gradle-9.6-error
git branch -D test/gradle-9.6-error
Test 2: Verify Dependencies Lock Detection
2.1 Create test branch

git checkout -b test/missing-lock-file
