find . -name "package-lock.json" -o -name "npm-shrinkwrap.json" | xargs rm
2.3 Commit and push

git add .
git commit -m "test: remove lock file for workflow testing"
git push origin test/missing-lock-file
2.4 Watch workflow run

Expected:
✓ Workflow detects missing lock file
✓ Creates bugfix/missing-dependencies-lock branch
✓ Opens PR with generated lock file
2.5 Clean up

git reset --hard HEAD~1
git push origin --delete test/missing-lock-file
git branch -D test/missing-lock-file
🔍 Troubleshooting Workflow Deployment
Issue 1: Workflow file not appearing in Actions tab
Solution:

# Verify file is in correct location
ls -la .github/workflows/fix-subertube-errors.yml

# Verify YAML syntax
yamllint .github/workflows/fix-subertube-errors.yml

# Try force-pushing
git push origin develop --force-with-lease
Issue 2: Workflow runs but gets stuck
Solution:

# Check Actions permissions in GitHub settings
# Ensure "Allow GitHub Actions to create PRs" is enabled

# Check branch protection rules
# May need to adjust "Require branch to be up to date"
Issue 3: Automatic PR creation not working
Solution:

# Verify GitHub token permissions
# Settings → Actions → Workflow permissions
# ✓ Read and write permissions
# ✓ Allow create and approve PR

# Check if branch is protected
# If yes, may need to allow exceptions for bot
