🔐 Security Considerations
GitHub Token Permissions
The workflow uses GitHub's default GITHUB_TOKEN which has:

✓ Read repo contents
✓ Create branches and PRs
✓ Write to Actions logs
✗ Cannot merge PRs automatically (safety)
Sensitive Information
DO NOT:
✗ Store API keys in workflow file
✗ Store passwords in environment variables
✗ Log sensitive GitHub tokens
✗ Commit .env files

DO:
✓ Use GitHub Secrets for sensitive data
✓ Mask secrets in logs
✓ Review all logs for accidental exposure
✓ Rotate tokens regularly
